{"step_index":134,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:51:34Z","content":"The existing **Brew & Bloom Café** project has been upgraded into a premium, responsive online food ordering and delivery platform.\n\nThe local preview server is active and running at **[http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)**.\n\n---\n\n### 🎨 1. Premium Visual Redesign & Palette\nThe design system features the requested high-contrast palette:\n* **Deep Forest Green** (`#073B32`) — Primary brand tone, sticky scrolled navigation, bestsellers backdrop, and administrative controls.\n* **Dark Espresso** (`#172421`) — Hero background, photo gallery, dark cards, and high-contrast typography.\n* **Vibrant Orange** (`#FF7629`) — Primary CTAs, Add-to-Cart buttons, active route polyline, and badges.\n* **Golden Yellow** (`#FFC247`) — Secondary CTAs, bestseller rankings, ETA highlights, and timeline progression.\n* **Warm Cream** (`#FFF8EC`) — Base menu surface and cart drawer background.\n* **Fresh Mint** (`#D9F3E5`) — Vegetarian badges and distance badges.\n* **White** (`#FFFFFF`) — Card bodies, modal containers, and inputs.\n* **Coral Pink & Lavender** (`#FF6B6B` / `#E5DBFF`) — Signature promotional category highlights.\n\n---\n\n### 🍕 2. Expanded Food Menu & Category Banners\n* **Central Editable Source**: All items, descriptions, tags, and prices are centrally managed in [`js/menu-data.js`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/js/menu-data.js).\n* **Categories Included**:\n  * **Coffee**: Espresso, Cappuccino, Café Latte, Americano, Mocha, Caramel Macchiato, Cold Coffee.\n  * **Tea**: Masala Chai, Ginger Tea, Green Tea, Lemon Tea, Iced Tea.\n  * **Cold Beverages**: Iced Latte, Chocolate Frappe, Oreo Shake, Strawberry Smoothie, Mango Shake, Fresh Lime Soda.\n  * **Quick Bites**: Veg Sandwich, Cheese Sandwich, Grilled Paneer Sandwich, French Fries, Peri-Peri Fries, Garlic Bread, Veg Burger.\n  * **Pizza & Pasta**: Margherita Pizza, Farmhouse Pizza, Paneer Tikka Pizza, White Sauce Pasta, Red Sauce Pasta.\n  * **Desserts**: Chocolate Brownie, Chocolate Lava Cake, Blueberry Muffin, Cheesecake, Chocolate Pastry.\n* **Interactive Features**: Real food photography for every item, vegetarian symbol badges, bestseller tags, instant keyword search, veg-only toggle switch, and sorting by price or popularity.\n* **Category Banners**: Banners for *Pizzas*, *Pastas*, *Frappes & Shakes*, and *Desserts* filter the menu with one click.\n\n---\n\n### 🛒 3. Functional Shopping Cart Engine\n* **Reactive State & Persistence**: Built in [`js/cart.js`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/js/cart.js), saving to browser `localStorage` across page reloads.\n* **Cart Drawer**: Smooth slide-in drawer accessible from the sticky navbar (with bouncing cart item badge) and footer.\n* **Live Calculation**: Dynamic subtotal, transparent 5% GST tax calculation, distance-based delivery fee (free above ₹500 within 3 km), and final payable total.\n* **Custom Notes**: Special cooking and packing instructions field.\n\n---\n\n### 🛵 4. Complete Checkout & Delivery Distance Engine\n* **Order Modes**: Choice of **Home Delivery**, **Self Pickup / Takeaway**, or **Dine-in at Café** (delivery fee automatically zeroed for pickup/dine-in).\n* **Location Options**:\n  * **Detect My Current Location**: Uses the browser's Geolocation API (`navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition`).\n  * **Manual Address Input**: Address fields with validation for 10-digit Indian mobile numbers (`^[6-9]\\d{9}$`) and 6-digit PIN codes.\n* **Interactive Leaflet Map**: Displays the Haldia Café location pin and a draggable destination pin. Automatically computes straight-line and estimated road route distance, checks against the 10 km delivery radius, and calculates the ETA.\n* **Payment Selector**: Clean selection between **Cash on Delivery** and **Instant UPI Payment** (with a clear demo mode indicator).\n* **Order Generation**: Generates unique order IDs (e.g., `BNB...`) and persists the order.\n\n---\n\n### 🗺️ 5. Live Delivery Tracking (`order-tracking.html`)\n* Accessible at **[`http://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html`](http://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html)**.\n* **6-Stage Visual Timeline**:\n  1. *Order received*\n  2. *Preparing your food*\n  3. *Ready for pickup*\n  4. *Picked up by delivery partner*\n  5. *Out for delivery*\n  6. *Delivered*\n* **Interactive Map**: Displays restaurant, customer destination, scooter icon, and route polyline.\n* **Telemetry Distinction**:\n  * **Demo Mode**: Features an explicit **`⚠️ DEMO TRACKING — NOT LIVE GPS`** pill and an interactive **Demo Stage Simulator** (\"Advance Stage\" and \"Drive Scooter\") to test rider animations.\n  * **Live Mode**: Subscribes to real-time coordinates streamed from the driver app.\n* **Partner Info**: Shows delivery partner name, vehicle details, verified badge, and direct call/WhatsApp buttons.\n\n---\n\n### 👨‍🍳 6. Order Management Dashboard (`admin.html`)\n* Accessible at **[`http://localhost:3000/admin.html`](http://localhost:3000/admin.html)**.\n* **Authentication**: PIN code protected (Default: **`brew2026`**).\n* **Operations**:\n  * Real-time metrics: Total orders, active kitchen queue, and sales revenue.\n  * Incoming order cards: Customer details, delivery address, instructions, items breakdown, and payment status.\n  * Status transition buttons (*Preparing*, *Out for Delivery*, *Delivered*, *Cancel*).\n  * Delivery partner assignment dropdown.\n  * Menu stock manager to toggle ingredients/dishes in and out of stock.\n  * Completed order history archive.\n\n---\n\n### 📱 7. Delivery Partner Fleet App (`driver.html`)\n* Accessible at **[`http://localhost:3000/driver.html`](http://localhost:3000/driver.html)**.\n* **Authentication**: PIN code protected (Default: **`driver2026`**).\n* **Features**:\n  * Mobile-optimized view showing the active delivery task.\n  * One-tap turn-by-turn navigation deep-link into Google Maps.\n  * **Genuine GPS Hardware Broadcast**: Toggles `navigator.geolocation.watchPosition` to stream real coordinates, speed, and accuracy to the backend.\n  * Status buttons: *Picked Up*, *Out for Delivery*, and *Mark Delivered (Cash Collected)*. Stops location sharing when delivery is complete.\n\n---\n\n### 🗄️ 8. Backend & Persistence Architecture\n* **Supabase Integration**: [`js/supabase-client.js`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/js/supabase-client.js) is configured to connect to Supabase or smoothly fall back to **LocalStorage Demo Mode** if credentials are not set.\n* **Database Schema Ready**: The complete PostgreSQL script is included in [`supabase-schema.sql`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/supabase-schema.sql) with tables (`orders`, `order_items`, `driver_locations`), Row Level Security policies, and Realtime publications.\n* **Zero Paid Dependencies**: Leaflet, OpenStreetMap, OSRM routing, and Supabase JS v2 operate without paid API keys.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Verification & Test Results\n\n```\nURL                                         Status\nhttp://localhost:3000                       200 OK  (Storefront, Menu & Checkout)\nhttp://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html   200 OK  (Live GPS Tracking Screen)\nhttp://localhost:3000/admin.html            200 OK  (Kitchen Admin Dashboard)\nhttp://localhost:3000/driver.html           200 OK  (Driver Dispatch Interface)\nhttp://localhost:3000/style.css             200 OK  (Design System & Animations)\nhttp://localhost:3000/script.js             200 OK  (ES Module Application Logic)\nhttp://localhost:3000/js/config.js          200 OK  (Central Configuration)\nhttp://localhost:3000/js/menu-data.js       200 OK  (Menu & Pricing Data)\nhttp://localhost:3000/js/cart.js            200 OK  (Cart Engine)\nhttp://localhost:3000/js/supabase-client.js 200 OK  (Backend Engine)\n\nNode.js ES Module Syntax Validation:\n✔ script.js syntax valid\n✔ js/config.js syntax valid\n✔ js/menu-data.js syntax valid\n✔ js/cart.js syntax valid\n✔ js/supabase-client.js syntax valid\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Deployment Instructions for Vercel\n\n1. Open a terminal in the project directory:\n   ```powershell\n   cd C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\brew-and-bloom\n   ```\n2. Deploy using the Vercel CLI:\n   ```powershell\n   vercel\n   ```\n3. For production release:\n   ```powershell\n   vercel --prod\n   ```\n\n*Refer to the complete artifact guide at [`brew-and-bloom-guide.md`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b76faff2-d711-4aab-931a-94ff7ee7f3a8/brew-and-bloom-guide.md) for full details on credentials, configuration options, and database setup.*"}
